 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? It depends on how much and what kind of riding you do. A few hours here and there on smooth paths probably not daily. The pressure should increase gradually, almost feeling the rubber stretching. If it feels like something burrowing its way through concrete, stop and check the valve. Squeezing is fine, as long as you stop if it feels wrong. Yes, pumping while riding down hill is not advised. Fill up completely and then add some air while stopped.",
